<title>SINGAPORE: TAIWAN TENDERS TO SELL SEPT 11-20 LIFTING FUEL OIL.</title>
<headline>TAIWAN TENDERS TO SELL SEPT 11-20 LIFTING FUEL OIL.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to sell 30,000 tonnes of 3.0-percent, 180-centistoke fuel oil for September 11-20 lifting, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on August 14 and bids will be valid until August 15.</p>
<p>In its last tender, Taiwan sold one cargo at around $100 per tonne on a free-on-board Kaoshiung basis.</p>
